+    \item \textbf{Throughput} ($Q$): vehicles leaving the network (via off-ramps and segment end) during the measurement period, counted by their exit time and scaled to veh/h.
+    \item \textbf{Average travel time} ($\overline{TT}$): mean time from entry to exit, over the same vehicles.
+    \item \textbf{Average delay} ($\overline{D}$): mean excess over free-flow travel, summed cell by cell as $D_i = \sum_{c} \max(0,\; \Tarr(c+1,i) - \Tarr(c,i) - \ell/v_f)$. Counting per cell rather than as total time minus distance over $v_f$ keeps the extra distance driven by a vehicle that missed its off-ramp out of its delay.
